$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: To a 25 mL three-neck round
bottom flask with a stir bar was added Pd(TFA)2 (33 mg, 0.1 mmol),
neocuproine (42 mg, 0.2 mmol), LiTFA (24 mg, 0.2 mmol) and NMP (1.5 mL).
The flask was evacuated briefly under vacuum, filled with oxygen gas and
sealed with a septum. A balloon was filled with O2 and connected to an
6-inch needle. The needle attached to the O2 balloon was inserted through
the septum, and the solution was sparged with O2 gas for ca. 10 min. A
solution of (E)- styrenylboronic acid (222 mg, 1.5 mmol) and allylbenzene
(132 μ L, 1 mmol) in NMP (1 mL) was added. The reaction was heated for 3
h at 40 °C using an oil bath with vigorous stirring under an O2
atmosphere supplied by the balloon. Pure product was isolated by using
the same procedure described above. The product yield obtained from the
reaction in a round-bottom flask (74% for 1 mmol scale in 3 hours and 64%
for 10 mmol scale in 6 hours) is lower than that observed using vortexing
agitation (88%) partly owing to the poorer gas-liquid mixing that takes
place in the former reaction. (Z)-5-methylenetridec-6-en-2-one 4i. Yield:
38%, 10 h, 14:1 regioselectivity, 3.5/1 Z/E. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
5.73 (d, J = 11.7 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (dt, J = 11.7, 7.5 Hz, 3H), 4.98 (s, 1H),
4.85 (s, 1H), 2.55 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.37 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H),
2.20-2.15 (m, 5H), 1.39-1.28 (m, 8H), 0.88 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 208.5, 144.3, 133.7, 129.3, 113.9, 42.6, 31.9, 31.4,
30.23, 30.19, 29.2, 28.9, 22.8, 14.3. HRMS (EI) Calcd. for C14H24O
([M]+): 208.1822, found: 208.1822.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Heck reaction, branched:linear=14:1, Z:E=3.5:1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalyst-Controlled Regioselectivity in the Synthesis of Branched
Conjugated Dienes via Aerobic Oxidative Heck Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zheng, Changwu; Wang, Dian; Stahl, Shannon S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
