$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(R*,E,E)-3-Benzylidene-1-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1-indanol [(R*,E,E)-17]:
According to the procedure described for (R,E,E)-13, Heck reaction of
(E,E)-8 (0.101 g, 0.207 mmol) with Pd(OAc)2 (2.3 mg, 0.010 mmol, 5.0
mol%), (R)-BINAP (9.6 mg, 0.015 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and 2,2,6,6-
tetramethylpiperidine (0.141 mL, 0.117 g, 0.825 mmol) in toluene (2.7 mL)
at 80°C for 15 h gave after purification by flash column chromatography
on silica gel (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1) (R*,E,E)-17 (0.061
g, 87%) as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by
HPLC analysis (26% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra,
(R*,E,E)-17 was isomerically pure.
(R*,E,E)-3-Benzylidene-1-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1-indanol [(R*,E,E)-17]: R
f=0.30 (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 3:1); HPLC (Daicel Chiracel AD,
n-heptane/i-PrOH 9:1, flowrate= 1 mL/min, λ=295 nm): t R=15.59 (major), t
R=22.61 (minor); [α]D 20=-12.6 (c=0.198, CHCl3, 26% ee); 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ=7.63 (dd, J=6.9, 0.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.44-7.48 (m, 3 H), 7.35-7.41
(m, 4 H), 7.31-7.35 (m, 3 H), 7.27-7.31 (m, 2 H), 7.23 (tt, J=7.1, 1.8
Hz, 1 H), 7.04 (dd, J=2.4, 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 6.52 (d, J=15.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.29
(ddd, J=15.8, 7.4, 7.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.42 (dd, J=16.9, 2.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.18
(dd, J=16.9, 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.83 (ddd, J=13.9, 7.6, 1.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.73
(ddd, J=13.9, 7.1, 1.3 Hz, 1 H), 2.29 (s, 1 H) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3): δ=148.1, 141.5, 139.0, 137.7, 137.3, 134.2, 129.0, 128.8, 128.7,
128.6, 128.6, 127.4, 126.8, 126.3, 124.9, 123.6, 120.8, 120.3, 81.6,
46.5, 45.2 ppm; IR (CHCl3): ν=3680, 3590, 3021, 1947, 1802, 1647, 1597,
1493, 1423, 1223, 1023, 924, 799 cm-1; MS (CI-NH3): m/z (%): 354 (2)
[(M+NH4)+], 321 (100) [(M-OH)+]; HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C27H20
[(M-H2O)+]: 320.15652; found: 320.15650.
