$DATUM A mixture of 26d (46.4 mg, 0.1mmol), PdCl2 (2 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol%),
PPh3 (5 mg, 0.02 mmol, 20 mol%), Cs2CO3 (82 mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5 eq),
norbornene (57 mg, 0.60 mmol, 6.0 eq), 8a (0.121 g, 0.6 mmol, 6.0 eq) in
1,4-dioxane (1.0 ml) in a schlenk tube was stirred at 85°C for 20 h.
After being cooled to room temperature the mixture was filtered through a
plug of Celite eluting with ethyl acetate (3×10 ml). The filtrate was
washed with brine (10 ml), dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography (10 % ethyl
acetate/ hexanes then 50% hexanes/ dichloromethane). 27d (15.1 mg, 33%).
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.45 (s, 1 H), 7.70 (bs, 1 H), 7.49 (bs, 1 H),
7.45-7.31 (m, 5 H),7.30-7.21(m, 2 H), 6.78 (s, 1 H), 5.79 (dd, J = 16.8,
10.4 Hz, 1 H), 5.16 (bs, 1 H), 4.98 (s, 2 H), 4.76 (bs, 1 H), 4.71 (d, J
= 17.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.18-3.99 (m, 1 H), 2.28 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H), 2.18-2.01
(m, 1 H), 2.01-1.85 (m, 2 H), 1.83-1.53 (m, 2 H), 1.67-1.53 (m, 1 H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 179.1, 172.8, 149.9, 138.9, 135.9, 133.4, 131.5,
130.7, 128.5, 128.4, 128.3, 128.2, 125.7, 124.1, 118.2, 66.3, 46.1, 32.0,
30.1, 29.2, 18.3; HRMS (ACPI) calcd for C27H27O5N2 [M++H] 459.1915, found
459.1919.
