$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Experimental Procedure for the
Oxidative Heck Active-Metal TemplateReaction: A solution of the alkene
half-thread (1 equiv.), boronic acid half-thread (2 equiv.), bipy
macrocycle (1 equiv.), Pd(OAc)2 (0.1 equiv.) and benzoquinone (1 equiv.)
in a 1:1 mixture of CHCl3/CH2Cl2 was allowed to stir under a balloon of
O2. After 72 h, a solution of KCN (10equiv.) in MeOH was added and the
resulting suspension allowed to stir at RT for 1 h. The solvents were
removed under reduced pressure and the resulting crude mixture dissolved
in CH2Cl2 and water. The aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (x3),
washed with brine and dried (MgSO4). Purification by column
chromatography (5:4.5:0.5 hexane:CH2Cl2:MeCN). Product, yield 30%.
Information present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Heck reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM [2]Rotaxanes through Palladium Active-Template Oxidative Heck
Cross-Couplings
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Crowley, James D.; Haenni, Kevin D.; Lee, Ai-Lan; Leigh, David A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2007), 129(40), 12092-12093

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME104 STEP1
