$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure for eq 3 and eq 4. In a
nitrogen-filled glovebox, Pd2(dba)3 (3.6 mg, 0.018 mmol) and
4’-chloroacetophenone (66 mg, 0.66 mmol) were added to a Tefloncapped
vial equipped with a stir bar. The Brønsted base (0.66 mmol of either
Cs2CO3 (220 mg) or Cy2NMe (130 mg)), P(t-Bu)3 (59 mg, 0.30 mmol), n-butyl
vinyl ether (8.2 mg, 0.0090 mmol), tetradecane (59 mg, 0.30 mmol;
internal standard for GC analysis), and dioxane (0.60 mL) were added via
syringe. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature. To measure
the yields of the Heck arylation product, aliquots were removed after 4
hours and after 32 hours of reaction, filtered through a plug of silica
with copious washings with Et2O, and analyzed by GC.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
