$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of 26b (40.4 mg, 0.10 mmol), PdCl2
(2 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol%), PPh3 (5 mg, 0.02 mmol, 20 mol%), Cs2CO3 (82
mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5 eq), norbornene (57 mg, 0.6 mmol, 6.0 eq), 8a (0.121
g, 0.6 mmol, 6.0 eq) in 1,4-dioxane (1.0 ml) in a schlenk tube was
stirred at 85°C for 20 h. After being cooled to room temperature the
mixture was filtered through a plug of Celite eluting with ethyl acetate
(3×10 ml). The filtrate was washed with brine (10 ml), dried over sodium
sulfate, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (10% ethyl acetate/ hexanes then 50% hexanes/
dichloromethane). Entry: 1 Product: 27a; Yield: <5%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Catellani reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed Chemoselective Catellani Ortho-Arylation of Iodopyrroles:
Rapid Total Synthesis of Rhazinal
