$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of phenyl trifluoromethanesulfonate with butyl vinyl ether
catalyzed by palladium acetate and 1,3-bis(diphenylphosphino)propane
(Scheme 4, entry 3e).8 Phenyl trifluoromethanesulfonate (113 mg, 0.50
mmol), butyl vinyl ether (55 mg, 0.55 mmol), and
N,N-dicyclohexylmethylamine (107 mg, 0.548 mmol) were weighed into a
small vial followed by addition of dioxane (0.5 mL). The resulting
solution was added to a vial containing palladium acetate (2.8 mg, 0.012
mmol) and 1,3-bis(diphenylphosphino)propane (5.8 mg, 0.015 mmol). The
mixture was stirred at 80 °C. After 5 h, an aliquot (30 μL) was diluted
in ethyl acetate and passed through a silica plug. The ratio of olefin
products (uncorrected) was then determined by gas chromatography.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Heck reaction, alternative preparation shown
