$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A Typical Procedure for Cobalt-catalyzed
Intramolecular Heck-type Reaction (Table 4 and 5). Anhydrous cobalt(II)
chloride (6.5 mg, 0.050 mmol) was placed in a 20-mL flask and was heated
with a hair dryer in vacuo for 2 min. After the color of cobalt salt
became blue, dppb (25 mg, 0.060 mmol) and THF (1 mL) were sequentially
added under argon at 25 °C. The mixture was stirred for about 5 min. A
blue mixture was obtained. Trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium chloride (1.0 M
THF solution, 1.5 mL, 1.5 mmol) was added to the mixture at 0 °C. After 5
min, iodo acetal 10a (0.18 g in 1.0 mL of THF, 0.50 mmol) was introduced
via syringe. The whole mixture was heated at reflux (bath temp. 80 °C)
for 5 min. The reaction mixture was poured into a saturated ammonium
chloride solution. The products were extracted with ethyl acetate (20 mL
× 2). The combined organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and was
concentrated. Careful silica gel column purification of the crude product
provided 11a (0.094 g, 0.42 mmol, 84%) and 12a (0.009 g, 0.04 mmol, 9%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cobalt-Catalyzed Trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium-Promoted Radical
Alkenylation of Alkyl Halides: A Complement to the Heck Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Affo, Walter; Ohmiya, Hirohisa; Fujioka, Takuma; Ikeda, Yousuke;
Nakamura, Tomoaki; Yorimitsu, Hideki; Oshima, Koichiro; Imamura, Yuki;
Mizuta, Tsutomu; Miyoshi, Katsuhiko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(24), 8068-8077

