$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Methoxy-N-(3-{4-[3-methyl-4(6-methyl-pyridin-3-yloxy)phenylamino]quinazolin-6-yl}-E-allyl)
Acetamide (30).
(6-Iodoquinazolin-4-yl)-[3-methyl-4-(6-methyl-pyridine-3-yloxy)phenyl]amine
28 (0.29 g, 0.6 mmol), N-allyl-2- methoxyacetamide 29 (0.171 g, 1.3
mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (0.040 g, 0.04 mmol), sodium acetate (0.15 g, 1.82
mmol), and triethylamine (1.3 mL, 9.3 mmol) were dissolved in ethanol (20
mL) and refluxed for 6 h. The reaction mixture was filtered to remove the
solid particles and the product solution evaporated under reduced
pressure (0.30 g, quantitative yield). The residue was purified using a
1:1:1 mixture of silica scavengers 1, 2, and 3 (0.5 g each). MS (ES+):
m/z = 470 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Heck coupling 1st step, supported reagent 2nd step, all three reagents
are used as scavengers in the 2nd step, 100% yield before scavenging,
without scavenging of Pd (2nd step) Pd 307 ppm, isolated product after
scavenging 4.8 ppm Pd
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Functionalized Sulfur-Based Silica Scavengers for the Efficient
Removal of Palladium Species from Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
