$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Example of the inversed Heck reaction on chip. 0.18 mg Pd(OAc)2, 0.63 mg
PPh3, 20.0 mg Bu4NBr, 5.0 mg 1-bromopyrene, 28.0μL Et3N and 100.0 μL
allyl acetate were dissolved in a 2:7:1 DMF/MeCN/H2O solution (1.5 mL).
The chip loaded with acrylate was submerged in this mixed solution and
selected cathodes were pulsed at a voltage of -2.4 V relative to a remote
platinum counter electrode for 0.5 sec on and 0.1 sec off. Following the
reaction for 6 minutes, the chip was repeatedly washed with EtOH and
prepared for pyrene-based fluorescent analysis.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM electrochemical, solid-supported reaction, voltage 0.5 sec on/0.1 sec
off, agarose-coated microelectrode-attached acrylic acid used, Heck
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Building Addressable Libraries: Site-Selective Use of Pd(0) Catalysts on
Microelectrode Arrays
