$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Heck Coupling of Bromobenzene-d5 with Methyl
trans-Cinnamate Procedure A. In a glovebox, Pd2(dba)3, the aryl or vinyl
halide, Cy2NMe, a solution of P(t-Bu)3 in dioxane, dioxane, and the
olefin (olefins that are solids were added prior to the addition of the
halide) were added in turn to a reaction vessel equipped with a stir bar.
The mixture was stirred at the indicated temperature for the indicated
amount of time. At the conclusion of the reaction, the mixture was
diluted with Et2O or EtOAc, filtered through a pad of silica gel with
copious washings, concentrated, and purified by column chromatography.
For experiments in which an internal standard was used, the internal
standard was added prior to the addition of the aryl or vinyl halide.
Entry 5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Versatile Catalyst for Heck Reactions of Aryl Chlorides and Aryl
Bromides under Mild Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Littke, Adam F.; Fu, Gregory C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
