$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the AHR: 0.033 mmol of
Pd(OAc)2 and 0.066 mmol of L*-1 or 0.099 mmol of L*-2 were dissolved
under Ar in 3 ml of dry and degassed solvent (see Table 1) and heated
under reflux for 1-2 h, until a clear yellow solution was obtained. 1.2
mmol of base, the appropriate additive and 0.33 mmol of 1 were added and
the mixture was refluxed for 48 h. The solvent was evaporated and the
crude product was purified by column chromatography (SiO2, Pet. Ether
40/60 : EtOAc = 9 :1). 4a-methoxy-4aH-benzo[c]chromen-2(6H)-one (2)
4a-isopropoxy-4aH-benzo[c]chromen-2(6H)-one (6) AHR was performed using
monodentate ligand L*-2, Pd(OAc)2 CHCl3 as a solvent and Cy2MeN as a
base, resulting in 100% conv. after refluxing for 48h. E.e. 93%. E.e.
determination on HPLC DAICEL OD column, Heptane: iPrOH = 95: 5, rt 12.6
min, 25.3 min. 1H NMR δ 0.82 (d, J = 6 Hz, 3H), 1.06 (d, J = 8 Hz, 3H),
3.83 (septet, J = 6 Hz, 1 H), 4.80 (d, J = 15 Hz, 1H), 5.11 ( d, J = 15
Hz, 1 H), 6.26 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1 H), 6.51 (s, 1H), 6.79 (d, J = 14 Hz, 1H),
7.04 (d, J = 8Hz, 1 H), 7.34 (m, 2H), 7.62 (d, J = 7Hz, 1H) 13C NMR δ
23,74 (q), 24.02 (q), 62.61 (t), 66.531 (d), 119.92 (d), 123.93 (d),
124.74 (d), 127.33 (d), 128.34 (s), 129.50 (d), 130.47 (d), 135.18 (s),
144.20 (d), 14834 (s), 156.29 (s), 183.27 (s). HRMS calcd. for C16H16O3
256.109, found 256.110.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, in-situ generated catalyst, Heck reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
