$DATUM 1,3,5,7-Tetramethyl-1-vinyl-1,3-dihydroindol-2-one (5a): To a dry flask
equipped with a stir bar was charged Pd2(dba)3 (9.2 mg, 10 μmol) and
(tert- Bu3PH•BF4 (11.6 mg, 40 μmol). The flask was capped with a septum
and backfilled with Ar. A solution of enantioenriched anilide (34.3 mg,
100 μmol) in degassed toluene (1 mL) was added by syringe, followed by
triethyl amine (33 μL, 14 μmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 24 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (5 mL)
and filtered through a pad of celite. The resulting solution was
concentrated in vacuo to generate a dark brown crude solid. The crude
material was purified by silica gel flash chromatography (hexanes/ethyl
ether, 6/4) to give a yellow oil.
1,3,5,7-Tetramethyl-1-vinyl-1,3-dihydroindol-2-one (5a), The atropisomer
(-)-(M) (99.5/0.5 er, first eluting enantiomer) yielded a yellow oil
(R)-(+) in 85 % yield (85.5/14.5, +37, c 7.3 mg/mL, second eluting
enantiomer). The atropisomer (+)-(P) (98.5/1.5 er, second eluting
enantiomer) yielded a yellow oil (S)-(-) in 92 % yield (86.5/13.5 er,
-38, c 8.9 mg/mL, first eluting enantiomer). IR (neat, KBr, cm-1) 2972,
2925, 1711, 1635, 1601, 1481, 1342, 1088; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.56
(s, 3 H), 2.23 (s, 3 H), 2.55 (s, 3 H), 3.48 (s, 3 H), 5.13 (d, J = 17.0
Hz, 1 H), 5.15 (d, J = 10.6 Hz, 1 H), 5.91 (dd, J = 17.0, 10.6 Hz, 1 H),
6. 83 (s, 2 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 18.9, 20.8, 22.7, 29.6, 50.6,
115.0, 119.5, 122.5, 131.9, 132.2, 133.6, 138.3, 138.5, 179.3; HRMS (EI)
calcd for C14H17NO 215.1310, found 215.1308; LRMS (EI) m/z 215 (M+, 100),
200 (58), 173 (46).
