$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Asymmetric Palladacyclization of Aryl Triflates
(GP1). A base-washed, oven-dried sealed tube equipped with a magnetic
stirring bar and a Teflon® seal was charged with the appropriate aryl
triflate (1 equiv), Pd(OAc)2 (1 equiv) and the appropriate chiral
bisphosphine (2 equiv). Deoxygenated N,N-dimethylacetamide (DMA,
distilled from CaH2 into a sealed tube under reduced pressure, backfilled
with Ar, then sparged with Ar for 2 h, 0.1 M) and
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (PMP, distilled from CaH2 under into a
sealed tube under reduced pressure, 4 equiv) were added to the solids. A
stream of Ar was bubbled through the resulting mixture for 15 min and
then the sealed tube was flushed with a steady stream of Ar for an
additional 15 min. The Teflon® seal was tightened and the solution was
maintained at 70-80 °C until the aryl triflate was no longer detected by
TLC analysis (typically 10-16 h). The solution was allowed to cool to
room temperature, diluted with EtOAc and poured into saturated aqueous
NaHCO3. The aqueous phase was separated and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated onto
silica gel. The residue was immediately purified by flash chromatography
eluting with diethyl ether-hexanes mixtures.Palladacyclization of 2 with
Stoichiometric Pd(0)·( R)-BINAP. Following GP1, a solution of aryl
triflate 2 (50 mg, 85 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (19 mg, 85 mmol), (R)-BINAP (106
mg, 170 mmol), PMP (53 mg, 340 mmol) and DMA (0.9 mL) was maintained at
80 °C for 14 h. After the usual workup, the residue was purified by flash
chromatography (50% diethyl ether-hexanes) to pure samples of 3β and 3α
(94 mg total, 81 mmol, 95%, 96:4 epimeric ratio) as bright yellow
powders: ( R)-BINAP Palladacycle (3β), yield (94 mg total, 81 mmol, 95%)
and ( R)-BINAP palladacycle (3α), yield (94 mg total, 81 mmol, 95%) (
R)-BINAP Palladacycle (3β). mp >150 °C, decomposition (Et2O-hexanes); 1H
NMR (500 MHz, THF-d8) δ 9.15 (t, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H, ArH), 8.84 ( br s, 1H,
ArH), 7.93-7.75 (m, 3H, ArH), 7.67-7.37 (m, 33H, ArH), 7.28-7.19 (m, 2H,
ArH), 6.31 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H, ArH), 5.82 (br s, 1H, ArH), 5.57-5.47 (m,
2H, ArH, CH2) 4.94 (d, J= 15.2 Hz, 1H, CH2), 4.40-4.33 (m, 1H, CH2),
4.02- 3.94 (m, 1H, CH2), 3.85-3.77 (m, 1H, CH2), 3.68-3.60 (m, 1H, CH2),
1.52 (ddq, 3J(H,P) = 20.2, 6.7 Hz, 3J(H,H) = 6.7 Hz, 1H, CH), 0.88 (ddd,
3J(H,H) = 6.7 Hz, 4J(H,P) = 8.4, 3.3 Hz, 3H, CH3); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
THF-d8) δ 181.43 (d, 3J(C,P) = 3.2 Hz), 181.08 (d, 4J(C,P) = 1.9 Hz),
154.47, 143.77, 142.81 (d, J(C,P) = 12.0 Hz), 138.60, 138.32, 138.19,
137.32 (dd, J(C,P) = 7.4, 3.7 Hz), 136.83, 136.73, 135.92, 135.66,
135.99, 135.39, 135.21-134.60 (m, 5C), 133.60, 133.55, 132.99, 132.76,
132.61, 132.51, 132.03, 131.81-131.49 (m, 3C), 130.73, 130.47, 130.09,
129.62, 129.42, 129.33, 129.15, 129.07, 128.94, 128.86, 128.80, 128.73,
128.67, 128.57, 128.48, 128.43, 128.38, 128.30, 128.17, 127.89, 127.83,
127.69, 127.44, 127.22, 126.86, 126.04, 125.95, 125.40, 124.33, 123.32,
122.39, 118.90, 109.44, 105.15, 79.64, 65.67, 64.36, 60.97 (br), 44.60,
44.28 (dd, 2J(C,P) = 99.4, 6.5 Hz), 19.83 (dd, 3J(C,P) = 4.2, 1.9 Hz);
31P NMR (202 MHz, THF-d8) δ 28.9 (d, 2J(P,P) = 49.6 Hz, 1.00P), 18.5 (d,
2J(P,P) = 49.6 Hz, 1.00P); [α=+191, [α= +208, [α= +282, [αand [αnot
possible due to sample absorbance (c = 0.41 in CHCl3); IR (thin film)
3053, 2957, 2926, 2853, 1695, 1668, 1594, 1482, 1432, 1339, 1293, 1177,
1123, 1096, 1000, 942, 911, 815, 741, 695 cm-1; LRMS (ESI+) Calcd for
C71H55N2O4P2Pd(M+H)+: 1167.3. Found: 1167.1( R)-BINAP palladacycle (3a).
mp >160 °C, decomposition (Et2O-hexanes); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.36
(d, J= 7.0 Hz 1H, ArH), 7.85-7.37 (m, 22H, ArH), 7.12-7.03 (m, 7H, ArH),
6.90-6.82 (m, 5H, ArH), 6.71-6.67 (m, 2H, ArH), 6.57-6.53 (dd, J= 12.7,
7.6 Hz, 2H, ArH), 6.42 (t, J= 7.4 Hz, 1H, ArH), 6.39 (t, J= 7.4 Hz, 1H,
ArH), 6.16 (br s, 1H, ArH), 5.97 (br s, 1H, ArH), 5.58 (d, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H,
ArH), 5.16 (d, J= 16.0 Hz, 1H, CH2), 4.45 (d, J= 16.0 Hz, 1H, CH2),
4.26-4.20 (m, 1H, CH2), 4.01 (q, J= 6.9 Hz, 1H, CH2), 3.84-3.81 (m, 1H,
CH2), 3.57 (q, J= 7.2, 1H, CH2), 2.02 (qdd, 1J(H,H) = 6.6 Hz, 3J(H,P) =
5.9 Hz, 3J(H,P) = 1.4 Hz, 1H, CH), 0.00 (ddd, 3J(H,P) = 12.4 Hz, 1J (H,H)
= 6.6 Hz, 3J (H,P) = 2.8 Hz, 3H, CH3); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 180.76
(d, 4J(C,P) = 3.8 Hz), 178.30 (dd, 3J(C,P) = 13.8, 1.3 Hz), 149.74,
142.83, 142.72, 141.82, 137.40, 136.37, 135.81, 135.60, 135.28, 135.18,
134.44, 134.37, 134.03, 133.99, 133.94, 133.90, 133.54, 133.46, 133.07,
